  "doc.title": "How Redis Answers in Microseconds · A Hands-on Essay",
  "doc.desc": "Send one SET user:42 \"alice\" or ZRANGEBYSCORE request and Redis's main event loop writes the reply back to the socket in microseconds. Following Redis 8.0 internals and specs, this essay unpacks that round-trip: the lock-free event loop, RESP2/RESP3 and pipelining, redisObject's 44-byte embstr cliff and listpack, progressive two-table rehashing, span-indexed ZSET skiplists, Redis 8 threaded network I/O, BGSAVE fork copy-on-write and multi-part AOF, active expiration and approximate LRU / Morris-counter LFU, 16,384 cluster hash slots and reverse-binary SCAN cursors, plus Vector Sets and shared-nothing frontiers. Eleven hands-on models run the exact underlying algorithms in the page.",
