  "ch5.limit": "With default seed 3 and 12 nodes, reaching rank 9 takes 4 hops. Small ZSETs under 128 entries and 64-byte members stay compact in `listpack` before converting to this `dict + zskiplist` pair.",
  "ch6.title": "I/O Bottlenecks & Redis 8 `io-threads`",
  "toc.ch6": "Threaded network I/O",
  "ch6.law": "At hundreds of thousands of operations per second, Redis spends up to 70% of its CPU in socket reads, RESP parsing, TLS, and reply writes; Redis 8 parallelizes network I/O across worker threads while keeping command execution strictly single-threaded.",
  "ch6.p1": "\"Redis is single-threaded\" is only half true. Redis 6 added I/O worker threads, and <strong>Redis 8.0</strong> shipped a revamped event-driven async <strong>`io-threads`</strong> architecture (still defaulting to `1` = off, commonly set to `4`–`8` on multi-core hosts, and now cleanly compatible with TLS). Each batch works in three phases:",
  "ch6.i1": "The main event loop assigns ready client sockets to `io-threads` workers, which read bytes and parse RESP frames (plus decrypt TLS) in parallel;",
  "ch6.i2": "Across a light synchronization barrier, the <strong>main thread executes every parsed command sequentially with zero locks</strong>;",
  "ch6.i3": "Workers take the resulting reply buffers and run TLS encryption and socket `write()` calls back out in parallel.",
  "ch6.p2": "Because `processCommand` itself remains serial on one core, throughput obeys <strong>Amdahl's Law</strong>: adding threads helps dramatically while socket I/O and TLS dominate, then flattens out once the single execution core hits 100%.",
  "dg.iothreads.cap": "Figure 6. Redis 8 threaded I/O: worker threads parallelize socket reads/parsing and reply writes around one lock-free command core.",
  "dg.iothreads.aria": "Diagram: three I/O workers on left reading/parsing in parallel, funneling into one single-threaded command core, then fanning out to write replies",
  "dg.iothreads.read": "Parallel read + parse + TLS",
  "dg.iothreads.main": "Exec loop",
  "dg.iothreads.wr": "Parallel write",
  "dg.iothreads.cap2": "I/O scales; command core sets Amdahl limit",
  "ch6.model.title": "Redis 8 io-threads Pipeline & Single-Core Ceiling",
  "ch6.model.how": "Slide \"io-threads count\" from 1 to 8 and adjust \"Payload size\" or toggle \"TLS encryption\" to watch when network I/O saturates versus when the single command core becomes the Amdahl ceiling.",
